Description: 0002-add-nc12-fourcc

From: HEVC enable on Pi 5
Subject: [PATCH] Add NC12 (Pi 5 column-tiled NV12) Fourcc mapping

Pi 5 rpi-hevc-dec exposes V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128 (fourcc 'N','C','1','2')
on its CAPTURE MPLANE queue. Without recognition, V4L2VideoDecoder::
SetupOutputFormat() rejects every enumerated CAPTURE format from
/dev/video19 and aborts decode init with "Failed to pick an output
format" — preventing chromium from ever HW-decoding HEVC on Pi 5.

This patch adds the bare minimum to get past format selection so that
runtime DMA-buf import behavior can be observed and characterised.

EXPERIMENTAL / KNOWN INCOMPLETE
NC12 is BCM2712 column-tiled NV12 (128-byte-wide column tiles), NOT
linear NV12. Mapping NC12 -> PIXEL_FORMAT_NV12 lies about the buffer
layout to chromium's media-layer code. Likely outcomes at runtime:
  * Clean DMA-buf import failure on the GPU side (Mesa V3D rejects the
    underlying buffer because it lacks DRM_FORMAT_MOD_BROADCOM_SAND128
    handling) — desired diagnostic.
  * Or silent visual corruption if some path treats it as linear NV12 —
    also useful information.
A complete fix requires plumbing the SAND128 modifier through
chromium's GPU import path, which is multi-week scope and out of band.

NC30 (10-bit V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_10_COL128) is intentionally NOT added.
The 8-bit case is sufficient to characterise the next blocker; mapping
10-bit column-tiled to PIXEL_FORMAT_P010LE would lie about layout AND
bit width, multiplying the surface area for confusion.

NC12 is also intentionally NOT added to GetPreferredRenderableFourccs
on Linux. We want chromium to fall back to a conversion / fail-fast
path rather than confidently telling the renderer "yes you can sample
this directly".

--- a/media/gpu/chromeos/fourcc.cc
+++ b/media/gpu/chromeos/fourcc.cc
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@ std::optional<Fourcc> Fourcc::FromUint32(uint32_t fourcc) {
     case P010:
     case MT2T:
     case BGR4:
+    case NC12:
     case AR24:
     case Q08C:
     case Q10C:
@@ -192,6 +193,13 @@ VideoPixelFormat Fourcc::ToVideoPixelFormat() const {
       return PIXEL_FORMAT_P010LE;
     case BGR4:
       return PIXEL_FORMAT_XRGB;
+    case NC12:
+      // EXPERIMENTAL: BCM2712 column-tiled NV12 from rpi-hevc-dec
+      // (V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128). Reported here as plain NV12 so the
+      // media layer's bit-depth / stride math accepts it. Underlying
+      // memory layout is column-tiled and will need GPU-side SAND128
+      // modifier handling to actually render correctly.
+      return PIXEL_FORMAT_NV12;
     case AR24:
       return PIXEL_FORMAT_ARGB;
     // V4L2_PIX_FMT_QC08C is a proprietary Qualcomm compressed format that can
@@ -296,6 +304,7 @@ std::optional<Fourcc> Fourcc::ToSinglePlanar() const {
     case MM21:
     case MT2T:
     case BGR4:
+    case NC12:
     case AR24:
       return Fourcc(value_);
     case YM12:
@@ -332,6 +341,7 @@ bool Fourcc::IsMultiPlanar() const {
     case P010:
     case MT2T:
     case BGR4:
+    case NC12:
     case AR24:
     case Q08C:
     case Q10C:
--- a/media/gpu/chromeos/fourcc.h
+++ b/media/gpu/chromeos/fourcc.h
@@ -103,6 +103,15 @@ class MEDIA_GPU_EXPORT Fourcc {
     // Single plane 8-bit little-endian XRGB (bytes in reverse B-G-R-X order).
     BGR4 = ComposeFourcc('B', 'G', 'R', '4'),
 
+    // EXPERIMENTAL — Pi 5 BCM2712 column-tiled NV12
+    // (V4L2_PIX_FMT_NV12_COL128). Two-plane 8-bit YUV 4:2:0 in 128-byte
+    // wide column tiles. Produced by /dev/video19 (rpi-hevc-dec). Mapped
+    // to PIXEL_FORMAT_NV12 at the media layer to pass format selection;
+    // this is a probing alias — the underlying buffer is NOT linear NV12
+    // and full zero-copy rendering also requires DRM modifier
+    // DRM_FORMAT_MOD_BROADCOM_SAND128 on the importing GPU side.
+    NC12 = ComposeFourcc('N', 'C', '1', '2'),
+
     // V4L2 proprietary format.
     // https://linuxtv.org/downloads/v4l-dvb-apis-new/userspace-api/v4l/pixfmt-reserved.html
     // Opaque format that can only be scanned out as an overlay or composited by
